Having obtained the wealth of others, one should not remember me in the beginning or in the end. Thus, O compassionate one, may you grant me much wealth. 20>. Meaning of the word

Adhanah - poor person; Ayam - this; Dhanam - wealth; Prapya - having obtained; Madhyan - being pleased; Uchchaih - excessive; Na - not; Mam - to me; Smaret - will remember; Iti - thinking thus; Karunikah - compassionate; Nunam - without doubt; Dhanam - wealth; Me - to me; Abhoori - something, a little; Na Adadhat - not given..

Thinking that if this poor fellow suddenly becomes rich, he will forget me in the intoxication of pleasure,
the merciful God has not given me even a little wealth. Meaning: From Sudama's statement that Lord Krishna did not give him even a little bit of wealth, this meaning
can be derived that instead of giving Abhuri—little, Ranch—wealth, God gave him his association
a vast treasure. Srila Viswanath Chakravarthy has suggested this alternative meaning. Thus, having contemplated, he attained the end of the world.
Surrounded by sun-rays, by the shining celestial bodies. 21). With the groves of the Vichitra-vriksha, with the herds of the Kuja-dvija clan. Prachalakamudambhakokhalotpalavaribhih. 22). With the lips, the breasts, the women, and the deer-eyed ones. Whose place is this, and how did it become like this? 23). Meaning of the word

